00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:18.130
Someone -- somebody wrote,
excuse me.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.802
This is a comment sent in.

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:25.037
"The running joke about this

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:28.908
being nominated for an Emmy
is thin at best."

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:35.281
But -- But it's not a joke.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:38.317
It did get nominated, twice.

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.119
Lost both times,

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:41.554
which felt like four times,

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:45.490
because of the recounts
I demanded.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:46.592
We always think
there's a chance,

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.761
even when they announce
somebody else.

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:50.296
I blame "La La Land"
or "Moonlight,"

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:54.000
whichever one you want to blame.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.002
But the older the person
reading your category,

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:59.504
the more you think,
"Well, hold on.

00:08:59.504 --> 00:09:01.140
Let's give it a beat."

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:07.312
The word is pronounced
"facultative."

00:09:07.312 --> 00:09:08.647
Said it wrong last week.

00:09:08.647 --> 00:09:12.385
"Facultative" means "occurring
optionally in response

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:16.389
to circumstances
rather than by nature."

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:18.557
For example, I'll use it
a sentence for you, Shoe.

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:20.993
"Leaving a snoozer
of a 'Corrections' comment

00:09:20.993 --> 00:09:23.195
like that is facultative."

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:28.067
Oh, um...

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:32.137
There's difference
between harakiri and seppuku.

00:09:32.137 --> 00:09:36.142
Harakiri is
the act of disembowelment.

00:09:36.142 --> 00:09:38.510
Seppuku is the whole ritual.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.181
And part of the ritual
is someone stands behind you,

00:09:42.181 --> 00:09:43.615
and after the disembowelment,

00:09:43.615 --> 00:09:47.853
they decapitate you
as an act of mercy.

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:50.856
And they say you can always tell
how your friends feel about you,

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:54.660
how quickly they volunteer
to do that part.

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.331
If you're like, "Well, bad news.

00:09:58.331 --> 00:10:00.365
I got my seppuku scheduled."

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:03.069
They're like, "I can be there."

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:04.603
I don't know if I have
any friends who would --

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:07.173
Oh, Samberg.

00:10:07.173 --> 00:10:09.941
"Uranus,"

00:10:09.941 --> 00:10:11.477
we're told,
the incorrect way to say it.

00:10:11.477 --> 00:10:12.845
Here's an interesting thing.

00:10:12.845 --> 00:10:14.513
And I looked it up, and I guess
there's some truth to it,

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:18.985
that Dan Rather didn't want to
say "Uranus" on television,

00:10:18.985 --> 00:10:21.753
so he started
calling it "Uran-us."

00:10:21.753 --> 00:10:23.556
Peter Jennings called it
"Ur-anus,"

00:10:23.556 --> 00:10:25.357
and Tom Brokaw called it --

00:10:25.357 --> 00:10:26.993
[ Garbled ] Uranus.

00:10:56.855 --> 00:11:01.893
I literally
just texted with him.

00:11:01.893 --> 00:11:03.528
[ Ringtone playing ]

00:11:03.528 --> 00:11:05.498
Oh. That's him.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:10.035
Hey, I just did my Tom Brokaw.

00:11:10.035 --> 00:11:12.905
Can you do your Brian Williams
for everybody?

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:15.341
-[ As Brian Williams ]
I'm Brian Williams.

00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:19.679
[ Laughter ]

00:11:31.924 --> 00:11:34.126
-It's really good.

00:11:34.126 --> 00:11:36.996
Ah.

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:40.266
Got a lot of suggestions
on how to stop chewing my nails.

00:11:40.266 --> 00:11:44.136
I appreciate it and want
to give each a fair hearing

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:46.005
and a meaningful response.

00:11:46.005 --> 00:11:48.073
"Try calcium magnesium
supplements."

00:11:48.073 --> 00:11:49.374
No.

00:11:49.374 --> 00:11:51.043
"When my daughter was young,
she used to chew on hers,

00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:52.778
so now we use Vicks VapoRub."

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:54.179
No.

00:11:54.179 --> 00:11:55.547
"I kicked the nail-biting habit
easily

00:11:55.547 --> 00:11:56.915
by getting braces on my teeth."

00:11:56.915 --> 00:11:58.250
No.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.885
"Seth, you got to cut
your nails and then paint them."

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:00.986
No.

00:12:00.986 --> 00:12:04.456
"I took bupropion
to quit smoking,

00:12:04.456 --> 00:12:05.991
and I quit biting my fingernails
after 50 years."

00:12:05.991 --> 00:12:07.159
No.

00:12:07.159 --> 00:12:10.495
Here's how I'm going
to stop chewing my nail.

00:12:10.495 --> 00:12:12.064
Willpower.

00:12:12.064 --> 00:12:14.833
And

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:17.336
so far, it's going pretty good.

00:12:17.336 --> 00:12:18.604
Let's take a look.

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:28.347 line:0%
[ Mumbling to self ]

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:32.017 line:0%
I guess that's about it.

00:12:32.017 --> 00:12:35.087 line:0%
See me next week.

